0 < 1 #!/usr/bin/env node
1 < 1 /**
2 < 1  * fleet/launch.mjs — start one run. The whole client, on the laptop.
3 < 1  *
4 < 1  * The order of a launch — validate, read, refresh the credential, push the
5 < 1  * plan to the evidence repository, then exactly one mutating lobby verb, `new`
6 < 1  * — and every literal it uses are `fleet/CONTRACT.md` §Launch order and
7 < 1  * §Literals; this header does not restate them (#1444). A refusal (exit 2)
8 < 1  * happens before anything is created; a failure after that (exit 1) prints the
9 < 1  * lobby's own words. Each phase's section comment below says why it is shaped
10 < 1  * the way it is.
11 < 1  */
12 < 1 
